e rows to digests (line 130)\n   └── unsafe { MH::compress_rows() }\n       ├── Hashes 2^k rows per digest\n       ├── Produces query_digest_layer of size (height / rows_per_query)\n\n2. Iteratively compress layers (lines 143-160)\n   while digest_layers.last().len() > 1 {\n       let prev_layer = digest_layers.last()\n       unsafe { MH::compress_layer(&mut layer, prev_layer, len) }\n       digest_layers.push(layer)\n   }\n   ├── Each layer is half the size of previous\n   ├── Continues until single root digest\n\n3. Copy root to host (line 163)\n   └── root = d_root.to_host()?.pop()?\n```\n\n**Instrumentation:**\n- `#[instrument(name = \"merkle_tree\", skip_all)]` (line 104)\n- `MemTracker::start(\"prover.merkle_tree\")` (line 118)\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Commitment Observation (Transcript)**\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/mod.rs`\n**Lines:** 118-156\n\n```\nAfter common_main_commit is obtained:\n  ↓\n  [Line 155] transcript.observe_commit(common_main_commit)\n  ↓\nLoop over per-AIR data (lines 131-175):\n  for (air_id, trace_ctx) in &ctx.per_trace {\n      Extract preprocessed_data commitment (if present)\n      Extract cached_mains commitments (per-AIR loop)\n  }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Key Findings on AIR Handling**\n\n**Per-AIR vs Batched Commitment:**\n\n1. **Common Main Traces:** **BATCHED into single commitment**\n   - All AIR traces are stacked together into one matrix\n   - Single `stacked_commit()` call produces one root\n   - All AIRs share the same NTT and Merkle tree computation\n\n2. **Per-AIR Cached/Preprocessed Traces:** **SEPARATE commitments**\n   - Each AIR's preprocessed trace: separate `stacked_commit()` call\n   - Each cached trace: separate `stacked_commit()` call\n   - Observed individually in transcript (lines 168-170)\n\n**Loop Structure:**\n```rust\n// Line 131 - Per-AIR iteration for metadata extraction\nfor (air_id, trace_ctx) in &ctx.per_trace {\n    // Extract log_height and cached_commitments\n}\n