e the large one runs, there's potential to save 10-30ms through overlap. This requires verifying that multiple commits actually exist per segment and would need moderate complexity in the commit orchestration layer.\n\nBut from the research, common main traces get batched into a single stacked commit, and per-AIR preprocessed traces are computed at keygen time, so there might only be one commit per segment at proving time. I need to check whether cached trace commits even happen during proving.\n\nAnother angle is reducing the GKR fractional sumcheck wall clock by cutting D2H sync overhead. The inner rounds currently synchronize the GPU-CPU boundary ~140 times, and even if each sync is only 5-10μs, that adds up to 1-2ms of cumulative overhead plus potential GPU pipeline stalls. Using pinned memory and async D2H transfers with CPU event polling instead of per-round cudaStreamSynchronize could recover 5-15ms on the Log variant.\n\nThat said, the probability of this being a real bottleneck is low since previous analysis showed the sync overhead was negligible, and the complexity doesn't justify the small expected gain. Not worth pursuing.\n\nI should look at the actual code to evaluate the next idea about pre-computing Round 0 Phase 1 static metadata at keygen time. Let me find the sumcheck_uni_round0_polys function to see what's feasible.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2279,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4057,"cache_read_input_tokens":107357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4057},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6755d07-23c8-46a3-81f0-36e3b63f2ed6","uuid":"bdf02211-ba66-4521-bcfd-195edc7e75e9"}
